concepts.content:
To recover the world coordinates for every pixel, we assume a pinhole camera model. Using the depth $z[n,m]$ and the intrinsic camera parameters $\mathbf{K}$, we obtain the 3D coordinates for a pixel with image coordinates $[n,m]$ in the camera reference frame as:

$$\begin{aligned}
\begin{bmatrix}
X \\
Y \\
Z 
\end{bmatrix}
= z[n,m] \times \mathbf{K}^{-1} \times
\begin{bmatrix}
n \\
m \\
1 
\end{bmatrix}
\end{aligned}$$

Note that $\mathbf{K}$ are the intrinsic camera parameters for the reference image.

